==Strategy==
==='''Chapter 1'''===
After the stage starts, send out meatshields to stall the Doge Dark for money. Kill it later on with a cheap damage dealer and send out [[:Category:Critter-class Cats|Critical Hitters]] (such as [[Jurassic Cat (Rare Cat)|Jurassic Cat]]) to kill the large amount of Metal Hippoes. Stack AoE Cats to fend off the Dark and Angel enemies and reach the base to secure your victory.

A high enough levelled [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Crazed Bahamut Cat]] (16~20+) can almost instakill the Gory Darks provided Bahamut hits them. Since Gory Dark has massive DPS, weakening them if you have enough meatshields and a Cat that can weaken Black (like [[Onmyoji Cat (Rare Cat)|Magica Cat]]) will help stop Gory Dark pushing your line back (provided they target the Gory Dark). Spamming lots of Dragon Cats can also stop the Gory Darks, Doge Darks and Gabriel from advancing by constantly knocking them back and eventually killing them.

==='''Chapter 2'''===
Just the same as Chapter 1, but there is a Dark Otter. Try freezing it or using status effects. Single Target units that have high damage (like [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Hip Hop Cat]]) can work against Dark Otter as well. [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]] stacking is also optional.

==='''Chapter 3'''===
At this point, you should have high leveled AoE attackers, because this level can be mildly difficult. Use the same strategy as Chapter 2 but more AoE attacking. Use [[:Category:Anti-Angel Cats|anti-Angels]]/[[:Category:Anti-Dark Cats|Dark]] to do this level if you have any, such as [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]].

